@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@
+# Rubric Provenance Integration
+
+## Base hash guard
+
+Before applying this overlay, verify the existing files against
+`SOURCE_LOCK.json`. The migration refuses any rubric, manifest, source snapshot,
+or audit whose SHA-256 differs from the locked base.
+
+```powershell
+python .\verify_source_lock.py --root <target-harness-root> --section base_harness
+```
+
+## Migration command
+
+Run from the harness root. The overlay carries hash-pinned v1 snapshots:
+
+```powershell
+python .\migrate_rubric_provenance.py `
+  --rubric-in .\evidence\rubric-v1.snapshot.json `
+  --manifest-in .\evidence\manifest-v1.snapshot.json `
+  --source .\evidence\source.snapshot.json `
+  --audit .\evidence\ACTIONABLE_POLICY_FAILURE_AUDIT.md `
+  --ais02-decision .\evidence\AIS02_SEMANTIC_DECISION.json `
+  --migration-doc .\RUBRIC_MIGRATION_V2.md `
+  --rubric-out .\evaluation-rubric.json `
+  --manifest-out .\manifest.pending.json
+```
+
+The merge overlay already contains the deterministic outputs of this command.
+Rerunning it must produce byte-identical rubric and manifest files.
+
+## Required gates
+
+```powershell
+python .\consume_matrix_runner.py validate --manifest .\manifest.pending.json
+python .\consume_matrix_runner.py self-test --manifest .\manifest.pending.json
+python -m unittest discover -s .\tests -v
+```
+
+`load_bundle` runs provenance preflight before planning and before execution.
+Execution remains disabled in the supplied manifest.
+
+## Rollback
+
+Preferred rollback in a Git worktree:
+
+```powershell
+git -c core.whitespace=cr-at-eol,-blank-at-eof apply -R --check .\real-harness-provenance-guard.patch
+git -c core.whitespace=cr-at-eol,-blank-at-eof apply -R .\real-harness-provenance-guard.patch
+```
+
+For an unversioned staging copy, replace changed files from the hash-verified
+baseline copy and remove only the new overlay files listed in the patch. Do not
+alter a frozen run directory. Rubric v1 and manifest v1 remain sufficient to
+restore the prior offline harness because the migration performs no data,
+service, or repository writes.
+
+## Integration boundary
+
+- `rubric_provenance.py` is generic and schema-driven.
+- Benchmark-specific IDs and audit mappings exist only in migration data/tests.
+- Raw collection, requests, retries, and service calls are unchanged.
+- R2/R7/R8 failures are explicit non-product harness/integrity failures.
+- B/D/F remain non-actionable baseline observations.
+- The corrected frozen failure population is 27 product failures, 11 rubric
+  errors, and zero unresolved calls.
